06/08/2026

o Read-only inspection of 'user_files' to collect the wall settings of the reaction
  CVs, for a comparison table against the pph3 and pph4 systems in the 'training'
  folder. No file was modified. I noticed a stale vim swap file
  '.plumed_ppimg2-TS.dat.swp' sitting in 'user_files', so that input may still be
  open in an editor somewhere; I left it alone.

o The CV names here differ from the ones used for pph3/pph4. The nucleophile
  coordination is 'coh' instead of 'cowh', the leaving group oxygens coordination is
  'colvp' instead of 'cobh', 'coelp' keeps its name, and the two distances are
  'delp_ob' (bridging O-P, the old 'dobp') and 'dnuc_elp' (nucleophile-P, the old
  'dowp'). Units are LENGTH=A and ENERGY=kcal/mol as in the other folder.

o Walls I extracted, lower/upper. For ppimg2-TS: coh 0.8/2.1, colvp -/1.1,
  coelp -/0.3, delp_ob -/3.2, dnuc_elp -/3.2. For ppimg2-hydrolysis the same
  coordination walls but the two distances open to -/3.5. In ppimg2-prod the
  nucleophile upper wall relaxes to 2.2 and 'delp_ob' switches sense, becoming a
  lower wall at 3.2 since the bond is already broken; 'dnuc_elp' carries no wall
  there. In ppimg2-react there is no 'coh' and no 'dnuc_elp' at all, colvp and
  coelp share an upper wall at 1.1, and the bridging distance is restrained from
  above at 1.7 under the name 'dob_elp'.

o The individual lower walls on 'colvp' and 'coelp' are absent in this system.
  Deprotonation is instead controlled collectively, through 'lw_1' acting on
  'copyro_tot' (the sum coelp+coh+colvp) at 1.8.

o The contrast with pph3/pph4 is large and expected: here coelp is capped at 0.3 and
  colvp at 1.1, against 2.1-2.2 and 3.1-3.2 in the protonated systems, because the
  pyrophosphate is fully deprotonated and its oxygens are coordinated to the two
  Mg rather than carrying protons. Consistently, the Mg are held close by
  'uw_dist' (all P-Mg distances below 3.5 A), the opposite of the pph3/pph4 setup
  where they are pushed beyond 6.5 A.
